A teammate proposes this to remove the server round trip. It lives in a React component that is bundled for the browser by Next.js:

const response = await fetch("https://llm-provider.example/v1/chat", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { Authorization: "Bearer " + process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_LLM_KEY },
  body: JSON.stringify({ model: "model-small", messages }),
});

.env.local (not committed to git):
NEXT_PUBLIC_LLM_KEY=prov_live_8f3c...

Statement: "The key stays secret because it is read from an environment variable in a file that is not committed to git."
